# ============================================================
#  The last day (playtest 2, X10; fills M21's stub). Month 48 is
#  Starfall of the final year and holds only pushed cards, in
#  priority order: the morning, the results, the career, the
#  lake, the people, the speech (expansion_y3.grim), the last
#  Starfall, what the yearbook keeps, and the eve of graduation
#  (calendar.grim). Every line of the yearbook is told here, and
#  where it is a choice the card makes it (feedback 2026-10-25):
#  the career you sign (took_<career>), whether you stay with a
#  partner, keep your friends, stand in the Dumonts' photograph,
#  write to Tamsin, and which personal lines the yearbook keeps.
#  Replaying this month alone reaches every ending the run can.
# ============================================================

@event last_morning
title: The Last Morning
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns
priority: 95
art: tower
tags: story
scene: A dormitory room in early light, trunks packed and strapped, graduation robes hanging on the wardrobe door, the towers gold through the window.
text: You wake before the bell, out of habit, and there's no bell. Your trunk is packed and strapped. The robes hang on the wardrobe door. It's Starfall, the last day of the year, and tomorrow you graduate. The castle is very quiet, as if it's listening.
> ok: Get up and begin the last day
  mood +tiny
  say: {has(origin_noble): You dress with care, the way you were raised to.|{has(origin_street): You check your pockets out of habit, then laugh at yourself.|You dress slowly, wanting the morning to last.}} The staircase that moves waits for you at the top, for once, as if it knows.

@event last_results
title: The Final Lists
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns
priority: 90
art: scroll
tags: story study
scene: A crowd of final-year students around a great oak door in the entrance hall, long lists of names pinned to it, one student reaching up to touch a line.
text: The final lists are pinned to the great hall door, and the whole year is crowded in front of them. {gpa >= 3.5: Your name is near the top, and someone has drawn a small star beside it.|{gpa >= 2.5: Your name sits in the middle of the list, solid and unremarkable, exactly where you hoped.|{gpa >= 2.0: Your name is near the bottom, but it's there.|Your name is on the list, just. Someone has pencilled "phew" next to it, possibly you.}}} {flag(thesis_distinction): In the thesis column, one word in gold ink, Distinction.|{flag(thesis_passed): In the thesis column, a plain pass.|{flag(thesis_resubmit): In the thesis column, in red, To be resubmitted.|}}}
> ok: Touch your name, for luck
  mood +tiny
  say: {gpa >= 3.0: People you barely know shake your hand on the way out. You let them.|{gpa >= 2.0: You run a finger along the line. Four years, one line. It's enough.|You stand there a while after the crowd has gone. It's on the list. It counts.}}

@event last_career
title: What Comes Next
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns
priority: 85
type: menu
art: letter
tags: story job
thread: careers
scene: Letters with heavy seals spread across the lid of a packed trunk, a student sitting cross-legged among them with a pen.
text: {has_offer(): Every letter you've had this year is spread across the lid of your trunk. Tomorrow you graduate, and today each of them wants its answer. You can sign one. You can, if you're brave or foolish, sign none.|No letter, no start date. Everyone else seems to know where they're going, or says so. The registrar's list is still pinned by her window, but you didn't put your name to it.}
> conclave: Sign with the Conclave
  hint: An apprentice at the Seven Towers.
  when: flag(offer_conclave)
  flag took_conclave
  mood +small
  say: You sign the Conclave's contract with the silver-sealed pen they sent. In the autumn you climb the Seven Towers in grey, an apprentice with seven years of wards ahead of you.
> royal_library: Sign with the Royal Library
  hint: A cataloguer in the old archives.
  when: flag(offer_royal_library)
  flag took_royal_library
  mood +small
  say: You sign for the cold room at the Royal Library Archives and the folios that object to being opened. You'll need gloves. You've bought two pairs already.
> fellowship: Take the Spire fellowship
  hint: A junior fellow among books that bite.
  when: flag(offer_fellowship)
  flag took_fellowship
  mood +small
  say: You chalk your name properly over the carrel at the Spire Library. A junior fellow, from the autumn: a life among books that bite, and secrets that wait.
> guild: Sign with the Guild's works
  hint: A journeyman's bench, two explosions a month.
  when: flag(offer_guild)
  flag took_guild
  mood +small
  say: You sign for the journeyman's bench at the Guild of Alchemists' works, and order the protective clothing on the same day.
> shop: Sign the harbour lease
  hint: A crooked shop and a still of your own.
  when: flag(offer_shop)
  flag took_shop
  mood +small
  say: You sign the lease on the crooked little shop by the harbour and hang the brass key back round your neck. In the autumn, the sign will read your name.
> unseen: Answer the Office of Unseen Affairs
  hint: A desk at an address that doesn't exist.
  when: flag(offer_unseen)
  flag took_unseen
  mood +small
  say: You write one word on a slip of paper and leave it under your pillow. In the morning it's gone. In the autumn, a desk at the Office of Unseen Affairs will be waiting.
> trading: Take the shipping house's desk
  hint: A partner's share of a harbour ledger.
  when: flag(offer_trading)
  flag took_trading
  mood +small
  say: You sign for the old partner's desk and his share of the ledger. The shipping house's anchor is pressed into the wax beside your name.
> teaching: Stay at Lumenhold to teach
  hint: The faculty barge, on the wrong side of the lectern.
  when: flag(offer_teaching)
  flag took_teaching
  mood +small
  say: You sign the faculty's contract in the staff room, at a desk with somebody else's initials carved in it. In the autumn you'll be on the faculty barge.
> circus: Join the Circus of Wonders
  hint: Wagons, crowds and illusions.
  when: flag(offer_circus)
  flag took_circus
  mood +small
  say: You sign the ringmaster's contract. In a week the circus wagons pass the village, and they'll slow down for you, and this time they'll stop.
> observatory: Go back to the plateau
  hint: Salaried chartmaker for the Observatory Expedition.
  when: flag(offer_observatory)
  flag took_observatory
  mood +small
  say: You sign for a salaried place with the Observatory Expedition and pack the frostbite remedies first. The plateau, and its nights, are yours from the autumn.
> field_station: Take the keeper's cottage
  hint: The Beastcraft Field Station, on the moors.
  when: flag(offer_field_station)
  flag took_field_station
  mood +small
  say: You sign for the keeper's post at the Beastcraft Field Station: a cottage, a lamp and more creatures than anyone could count.
> thornwick: Cross the hills to Thornwick
  hint: A researcher's bench at the rival academy.
  when: flag(offer_thornwick)
  flag took_thornwick
  mood +small
  say: You sign Thornwick's contract in green ink. In the autumn you'll cross the hills, and Lumenhold will say something cutting, and you'll go anyway.
> spire: Stay on in the Spire's stacks
  hint: A keeper of the stacks, full time.
  when: flag(offer_spire)
  flag took_spire
  mood +small
  say: You leave your signature under the bell on the reference desk. In the autumn you'll be back behind it, with a longer ladder.
> newt: Stay on at the Gilded Newt
  hint: Behind the bar, then in charge of it.
  when: flag(offer_newt)
  flag took_newt
  mood +small
  say: You shake on it over the bar with the landlady, properly this time. Full time from the autumn, and in charge in a year or two.
> pell: Stay on at Pell & Daughters
  hint: The counter, and one day the drawers.
  when: flag(offer_pell)
  flag took_pell
  mood +small
  say: You sign Pell's ledger under his daughters' names. Old Pell stops counting long enough to watch you do it, then starts again from one.
> courier: Keep your courier's satchel
  hint: Flying the lake in all weathers.
  when: flag(offer_courier)
  flag took_courier
  mood +small
  say: You hang the satchel with your name on it back on its peg, where it will be in the autumn, and the autumn after that.
> clerk: Take the registrar's clerk's desk
  hint: Stamps, ledgers and a window on a wall.
  when: flag(offer_clerk)
  flag took_clerk
  mood +tiny
  say: You sign for the clerk's desk at the registrar's window. It pays the rent. It is a start date. Today that is enough.
> look: {has_offer(): Sign none of them, and keep looking|Keep looking}
  hint: {gpa >= 2.5 or renown >= 30: Your grades and your name will open doors, in time.|Without a post, it's home for a while.}
  flag took_none
  mood -tiny
  say: {gpa >= 2.5 or renown >= 30: You put the pen down. Your grades are good and people know your name; the world can make you a better offer in its own time. You'll rent a room and write letters.|You put the pen down, and the letter you'll write home is the hardest you've ever had to write. There's a room there, and a bed that's too short, and time.}

@event last_lake
title: The Lake, One Last Time
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns
priority: 80
art: wave
tags: story mystery
scene: A student standing alone at the end of a wooden jetty at dawn, the Mirror Lake perfectly still, the towers reflected upside down in it.
text: You walk down to the lake before breakfast, the way you did your first morning. {flag(hollow_sealed): It's clearer than you've ever seen it, clear all the way down, and nothing looks back. You did that. Almost nobody knows.|{flag(hollow_freed): It has been different since the spring it froze, warmer somehow, and the candles along the shore lean toward you as you pass. You did that too.|{flag(hollow_bargain): The water is still. The mark on your palm is not. It hums as you come near, like something greeting something.|{flag(hollow_fled): The water looks ordinary. It isn't. Somewhere under it a door stands ajar, because you ran, and the headmistress's hair has been white since that night.|{flag(hollow_held_line): The first-years you held the tower for are skimming stones off the jetty. One of them waves at you. Whatever happened under the ice that night, it happened without you, and they are alive.|{flag(hollow_failed): It's calm this morning. You know what lies beneath it, and who paid to keep it closed. You stand on the jetty a long time.|{clues(hollowstar) >= 1: There were stories about this lake, and you followed some of them a little way. You never learned what they meant, or whether they meant anything. The lake isn't telling.|It's flat and blue and ordinary, and the towers stand upside down in it. Four years, and it never once did anything strange. That you saw.}}}}}}}
> ok: Say goodbye to the lake
  mood +tiny
  say: {~You skim one stone. It skips seven times, which is your record, and nobody saw.|You crouch and put your hand in the water. It's cold, the way it always was.} Then you walk back up to the castle without looking round.

@event last_friends
title: The Last Ordinary Morning
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns
priority: 75
cast:
  friend: any where rel(friend) >= 15 and not tagged(friend, outsider)
art: cup
tags: story social
scene: Two students sitting on the rim of a courtyard fountain with mugs of tea, packed trunks stacked by the doors behind them.
text: {friend} finds you in the courtyard with two mugs of tea and no particular reason. "Last ordinary morning," {they} say{s}. "I thought it should be spent properly." {bonds(friend) + bonds(close) >= 3: The others drift over one by one, the friends who stayed, until the fountain's rim is full.|You sit on the rim of the fountain and don't talk about tomorrow.}
> left: Promise to visit, and mean it
  hint: {bonds(friend) + bonds(close) >= 3: The yearbook will remember the ones who stayed.|A date, a place and a time.}
  flag kept_friends
  rel friend +small
  mood +small
  say: You set a date, a real one, with a place and a time, and write it in every notebook round the fountain. {friend} underlines it twice. You all know which of you will be late.
> right: Say goodbye properly, here
  hint: A clean farewell, and no promises to break.
  rel friend +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: You give {friend} the thing on your desk you'd most miss: a cracked mug, a dog-eared book, the stone from the lake. No promises; you've both seen what happens to promises. {They} turn{s} it over and over and say{s} nothing, which says enough.

@event last_partner
title: After Tomorrow
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns
priority: 72
cast:
  partner: any where bond(partner) == "partner"
per: partner
art: heart
tags: story romance
scene: Two students sitting on a castle battlement at noon, legs dangling over the edge, a map of the realm spread between them, weighted with an apple.
text: {partner} has a map, an apple and the whole afternoon. "Tomorrow we're not students," {they} say{s}. {flag(after_together): "We said we'd go together. I still mean it. Do you?"|"So I thought we'd better have a plan. Or decide that we don't have one."} The map is spread on the battlement between you, weighted at one corner with the apple.
> left: Plan the first year together
  hint: Whatever comes, together.
  spark partner +small
  mood +small
  queue last_partner now
  say: You plan it badly and in detail: a town on the map, a room above a shop, whose turn it is to cook. {partner} draws a circle round the town in ink, so it can't be rubbed out.
> right: Part at the gate tomorrow
  hint: Kindly, and for good.
  bond partner ex
  mood -medium
  alignment +tiny
  queue last_partner now
  say: You tell {partner} the truth: that tomorrow you'll walk out of the gates in different directions, and that it's right. {They} fold{s} the map very carefully and give{s} you the apple. Neither of you eats it.

@event last_rival
title: One Last Word
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns
priority: 70
cast:
  rival: any where bond(rival) == "rival" or bond(rival) == "nemesis"
art: wand
tags: story social
scene: Two students facing each other in an empty duelling hall, wands holstered, packed trunks visible through the open door behind them.
text: {rival} is waiting in the empty duelling hall, as if by appointment. Four years of grudges, and tomorrow there won't be a school to have them in. "Well," {they} say{s}. "That's that, then."
> left: Offer your hand
  rel rival +medium
  mood +small
  say: {rival} looks at your hand for a long moment, then takes it, hard. "You were worth beating," {they} say{s}, and then, almost too quietly to hear, "and worth losing to."
> right: "Rematch, in ten years."
  rel rival +small
  renown +tiny
  say: "Ten years," says {rival}, "and I'll still win." You shake on it in front of the last of the Circle, who spread it round the year by supper. It's the closest either of you will come to saying anything kind.

@event last_starfall
title: The Last Starfall
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns
priority: 62
art: star
tags: festival story
scene: Final-year students in a row on the observatory roof under a sky full of falling stars, graduation robes thrown over their shoulders like blankets.
text: Tonight is Starfall, and by tradition the final-years have the observatory roof to themselves. The first-years are down on the lawns with their jars. Up here, everyone is pretending not to be sad.
> left: Catch one for the road
  challenge feat apprentice slim luck:
    win:
      mood +small
      renown +tiny
      say: It drops into your hands with a hiss, the last thing Lumenhold gives you. The whole roof cheers. You'll keep it in its jar on a windowsill somewhere you haven't seen yet.
    lose:
      mood +tiny
      say: You lunge, miss, and sit down hard, and the whole roof laughs, and you laugh too. Some things you're supposed to leave behind.
> right: Lie back with everyone
  mood +medium
  say: You lie in a row with your year, shoulder to shoulder, and count the stars aloud until the counting falls apart. Somebody starts to cry, and then everybody is laughing.

@event last_dumonts
title: Two Pale Heads
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns and met(kael) and (flag(dumont_reunited) or flag(ilse_taken))
priority: 71
art: snow
tags: story social
scene: A photographer's tripod on the great hall steps, graduates jostling into rows, a pale young man at the end of a row beside an empty space.
text: {flag(dumont_reunited): The photographer is herding the year onto the great hall steps. At the end of a row, two pale heads lean together, Kael and Ilse, who was raised to open the door he refused. Kael sees you and moves up, which leaves a space between them and the edge.|The photographer is herding the year onto the great hall steps. At the end of a row Kael stands beside a space nobody is allowed to fill. Ilse should be in it. The man in grey took her north, and no letter has come.}
> left: {flag(dumont_reunited): Squeeze into the photograph with them|Leave the space empty with him}
  hint: The yearbook will keep this.
  rel kael +small
  if flag(dumont_reunited):
    flag kept_dumonts
    say: You squeeze in beside them, and Ilse elbows you, and Kael, for once, laughs out loud just as the shutter goes. It's the only photograph of the three of you, and it hangs in two houses for the rest of your lives.
  else:
    flag kept_ilse_chair
    say: You stand at the edge of the space, so it stays a space, and Kael's hand finds your shoulder for a moment. In the photograph there's a gap in the row the size of a girl in white furs.
> right: {flag(dumont_reunited): Take the photograph yourself|Talk Kael into closing the gap}
  hint: Today, and not the yearbook.
  mood +small
  if flag(dumont_reunited):
    say: You take the camera from the photographer and make them stand still for once. Two Dumonts, squinting at the sun, in nobody's photograph but yours.
  else:
    rel kael +small
    say: "She'd hate being a gap," you tell him, and he almost smiles, and moves up. In the photograph the row closes. Neither of you forgets why it was open.

@event last_tamsin
title: A Page for Thornwick
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns and flag(tamsin_friends) and rel(tamsin) >= 15
priority: 69
art: letter
tags: story letter
scene: A yearbook page and a sheet of green-sealed paper side by side on a desk, a student holding a pen over both.
text: There's a space in the corner of your yearbook page where a friend's message should go, and a green-sealed letter on your desk that came this morning: "Four years of rivalry, four hundred letters. Leave me the corner. Insufferable to the end, T."
> left: Leave Tamsin the corner
  hint: The yearbook will keep this.
  flag kept_tamsin
  rel tamsin +small
  say: You send the page over the hills by the evening owl. It comes back by morning, a green seal pressed into the corner, which is not allowed, and two lines you'll know by heart for the rest of your life.
> right: Save it for the spring meeting
  hint: Biscuits, halfway between, every spring.
  mood +small
  say: You write back that the corner can wait: you'll fill it in person, at the town halfway between, in the spring, with biscuits. Tamsin's reply says "Coward" and "Yes" in the same line.

@event last_remembered
title: What the Yearbook Keeps
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns and ((renown >= 45) or (alignment >= 60) or (alignment <= -60) or flag(thesis_hollowstar))
priority: 61
type: menu
pick: 2
art: book
tags: story
scene: A yearbook committee's table in the library, proofs of portrait pages spread out, a student reading their own page upside down.
text: The yearbook committee has your page in proof, with the lines they mean to print under your portrait. You may let them stand or strike them out. "Two at most," says the editor, a second-year with ink on her nose. "We're short of room."
> renown: Let them print your fame
  hint: The most talked-about student in a generation.
  when: renown >= 45
  flag remember_renown
  say: You leave the line about the Ledger's special edition. The editor looks relieved; it was her favourite.
> lumen: Let them print the line about you
  hint: "The one you went to when it mattered."
  when: alignment >= 60
  flag remember_lumen
  say: Someone has written "The one you went to when it mattered." You don't know who. You leave it.
> hollow: Let the shadow stand
  hint: The candles behind your portrait went out.
  when: alignment <= -60
  flag remember_hollow
  say: In the proof, the candles behind your portrait have gone out. The editor offers to retouch it. You tell her to leave it as it is.
> thesis: Keep the line about your thesis
  hint: The thesis they locked away.
  when: flag(thesis_hollowstar)
  flag remember_thesis
  say: The line about your thesis on the founders' seal has been half struck through already, in the headmistress's hand. You un-strike it.
> plain: Strike them all
  hint: Just your name, and the year.
  mood +tiny
  say: You strike out every line. The editor sighs and prints your name and the year, and nothing else. It suits you, somehow.
